# PCB Lab Templates: Copper Layer Usage

When authoring or fixing PCB lab templates (`tools/pcb_templates/`, `lab_*.pcbsim`):

1. **Every copper layer must carry traces** — do not leave In1/In2/In3/In4 (or B) empty when Cu≥4/6/8. Prefer assigning real nets to each layer rather than dummy stubs.
2. **Complex boards → more layers** — if signals conflict on F/B, raise Cu (4→6→8) and split roles (e.g. power H / power V / signal H / signal V).
3. **Avoid same-layer H∩V crosses** — put horizontals and verticals of different nets on different copper layers when possible.
4. Target **cross≈0 / clash≈0** after hand layout; sync `Test_Template/` and `entry/.../rawfile/Test_Template/`.
